<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ireland's ACC Bank raises variable rates.</title>
<headline>Ireland's ACC Bank raises variable rates.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's ACC Bank said on Friday that it was raising its variable rates with effect from close of business on May 9.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement it was raising its standard home loans rate to 7.95 percent from 7.45 percent.</p>
<p>The move follows a 50 basis point rise in the official Short Term Facility Rate (STF) by the central bank on May 1.</p>
<p>A number of other lending institutions, including Irish Permanent, Allied Irish Banks, Bank of Ireland and First National Building Society, have already raised their rates.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
